<Step enable="True" id="89" name="# (comment)"><DisableStepCollapsed state="False"/><Restore state="False"/><Text>Description: reports voided session notes, one row per voided original, beside the note that replaced it.</Text></Step>
<Step enable="True" id="89" name="# (comment)"><DisableStepCollapsed state="False"/><Restore state="False"/><Text>PARAMETER mode "batch" (default) - {"folder": "&lt;folder ending in a slash&gt;"}
  Called at the end of the billing export (Manage: Export, sessionNotes) AFTER that batch is marked exported. Writes revisions.xlsx for the billing team and marks each row voidReported so it is only sent once.
PARAMETER mode "range" - {"mode": "range", "startDate": "9/1/2026", "endDate": "9/30/2026"}
  Called from the client app's Export dialog (Voided Notes Report). Every note VOIDED in the date range, whether or not billing has seen it. Asks for a folder, writes VoidedNotes_&lt;start&gt;_to_&lt;end&gt;.xlsx and changes nothing.
RESULT: number of rows written</Text></Step>
<Step enable="True" id="89" name="# (comment)"><DisableStepCollapsed state="False"/><Restore state="False"/><Text>Batch mode reports a voided original only when:
- it had itself been exported (billing never saw one that was not - nothing to void), and
- the revision that finally replaced it has been exported too, so billing receives the void and the replacement together. A revision still waiting on signatures holds its row back to a later batch.
Both modes follow a revision chain to the newest note.</Text></Step>
